  <p><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Integer" target="_blank">[integer</a> extended]</p>
  <p><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/FALSE" target="_blank">[FALSE</a>]</p>
  <p>If <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/TRUE" target="_blank">TRUE</a> llHTTPRequest will always return a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Key" target="_blank">key</a>. If there was an error making the HTTP request. Detailed error information will be returned through the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Http_response" target="_blank">http_response</a> event using the provided key. Error information is delivered in a JSON block as described in <a href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7807" target="_blank">RFC 7807</a>. Details about extended return codes can be found below.</p>
